
3
Colors & fonts — one file to edit
essential_viewer/user/custom.css Key file
This is the official customization file — explicitly documented by Essential Project. It overrides the default theme without touching core files. If the file is empty, add your rules.
Edit this file
/* ============================================ YOUR BRANDING — edit values below only ============================================ */

/* 1. Header background color */
.navbar, .navbar-default, #header, .eas-header {
  background-color: #003087 !important; /* ← your primary color */
}

/* 2. Header logo — swap image */
.navbar-brand img, .eas-logo img, #logo img {
  content: url('../user/images/your-logo.png');
  max-height: 40px;
  width: auto;
}

/* 3. Navigation link colors */
.navbar-default .navbar-nav > li > a {
  color: #ffffff !important; /* ← nav text */
}
.navbar-default .navbar-nav > li > a:hover {
  color: #ccddff !important;
}

/* 4. Primary accent / buttons */
.btn-primary, .eas-btn-primary {
  background-color: #003087 !important;
  border-color: #002060 !important;
}

/* 5. Sidebar/panel highlight */
.eas-sidebar-header, .panel-heading {
  background-color: #003087 !important;
  color: #ffffff !important;
}

/* 6. Page title / header text */
.eas-page-title, h1.report-title {
  color: #003087 !important;
}

/* 7. Optional: change font */
body, .navbar {
  font-family: 'Arial', sans-serif !important;
}
Replace the #003087 values with your own brand hex colors. Use your browser's DevTools (F12) on a live viewer page to identify exact CSS selectors if these need tweaking for your version.
4
App title (browser tab & page title)
essential_viewer/WEB-INF/web.xml
Changes the application display name shown in browser tabs and server admin panels.
Edit this file
<!-- Find this line: -->
<display-name>Essential Viewer</display-name>

<!-- Change to: -->
<display-name>Your Company EA Portal</display-name>
5
Repackage & redeploy
# Go into the extracted folder
cd /path/to/tomcat/webapps/essential_viewer/

# Repackage as a WAR
jar -cvf ../essential_viewer_branded.war .

# Restart Tomcat to pick up changes
./bin/shutdown.sh && ./bin/startup.sh
Shortcut: If Tomcat is already running with the extracted folder (no WAR needed), you only need to restart Tomcat after editing — no repackaging required.
